  "answer": "### Short Answer\nA VAT-registered exporter that sells 100% of its goods abroad can obtain a refund or tax credit for input VAT. This is provided under the provisions of the NIRC that allow for the refund of input VAT on zero-rated sales.\n\n### Interpretation\n\n### Practical Meaning\nFor VAT-registered exporters, this provision is beneficial as it allows them to recover input VAT, thereby improving cash flow and reducing the overall tax burden. It is essential for exporters to maintain proper documentation and comply with the filing requirements to successfully claim these refunds or credits. This mechanism supports the competitiveness of exporters in the global market by alleviating the VAT cost on their inputs.",
